# Story 9: Session Persistence (45s)
# Hook: Detach, reboot, reattach -- your panes come back exactly as you left them.
# Duration: 45s
# Source: story-009-session-persistence.tape
#
# Voiceover script with timing cues.
# Format: [START --> END] narration text
# Each entry should be spoken within its time window.
# Gaps between entries are silent (viewer watches the demo).
#
# Total segments: 5

[00:00.0 --> 00:05.0]
Detach, reattach -- your panes come back exactly as you left them.

[00:05.0 --> 00:15.0]
Every session's state lives on disk under ~/.local/state/rysh/nats, one directory per session.

[00:15.0 --> 00:26.0]
Inside, two JetStream key-value buckets hold everything: rysh-workspace stores your tab and pane layout...

[00:26.0 --> 00:36.0]
...and rysh-panes stores each pane's output buffer, mode, and last command, keyed by pane ID.

[00:36.0 --> 00:45.0]
On attach, the workspace restores straight from KV. Detach freely -- nothing is lost.

